"First, let's expand the product \\((x-2)^2(x+2)^2\\).\n\n\\[\n(x-2)^2 = x^2 - 4x + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n(x+2)^2 = x^2 + 4x + 4\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply these two expressions:\n\n\\[\n(x^2 - 4x + 4)(x^2 + 4x + 4) = x^4 + 4x^3 + 4x^2 - 4x^3 - 16x^2 - 16x + 4x^2 + 16x + 16\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= x^4 + 0x^3 - 12x^2 + 0x + 16\n\\]\n\nThe nonzero coefficients are 1, -12, and 16. The product of these coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n1 \\times (-12) \\times 16 = -192\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the nonzero coefficients is \\(\\boxed{-192}\\)."
