"To determine the least number of main courses the restaurant should offer so that a customer could have a different dinner each night in the year 2003, we need to calculate the total number of possible dinner combinations and ensure it is at least 2003.\n\nLet's denote the number of main courses by \\( m \\). Then, the number of appetizers is \\( 2m \\). The number of desserts is given as 3.\n\nThe total number of possible dinner combinations is the product of the number of appetizers, main courses, and desserts:\n\\[\n2m \\times m \\times 3 = 6m^2\n\\]\n\nWe need this product to be at least 2003:\n\\[\n6m^2 \\geq 2003\n\\]\n\nFirst, divide both sides by 6:\n\\[\nm^2 \\geq \\frac{2003}{6} = 333.83\n\\]\n\nNext, take root the square root of both sides:\n\\[\nm \\geq 18\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the least number of main courses the restaurant should offer is \\(\\boxed{18}\\)."
