"The binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is defined as:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 13!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator. Notice that $31! = 31 \\times 30 \\times 28!$, and $13! = 13 \\times 12 \\times 11 \\times \\cdots \\times 1$. Therefore, we can write:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 13!}\n\\]\n\nThe $28!$ terms cancel out, leaving us with:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30}{1 \\times 13} = 465\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is $\\boxed{465}$."
