"To determine the number of handshakes at a party where 10 people attend and everyone shakes hands with everyone else, we can use the concept of combinations. Specifically, we need to find the number of ways to choose 2 people out of 10 to shake hands. This can be calculated using the combination formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the total number of people, and \\( k \\) is the number of people involved in each handshake. In this case, \\( n = 10 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10!}{2! \\cdot 8!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 8!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = \\frac{90}{2} = 45\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of handshakes is \\boxed{45}."
