"First, we calculate the product \\(10 \\times 15 \\times 24\\):\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 15 = 150\n\\]\n\\[\n150 \\times 24 = 360\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the positive square root of 360:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{360} = \\sqrt{120 \\times 3} = \\sqrt{120} \\times \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify \\(\\sqrt{120}\\) and \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{120} = \\sqrt{10 \\times 12} = 10\\sqrt{12}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{360} = 10\\sqrt{12} \\times \\sqrt{3} = 10\\sqrt{36}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\)."
