"To determine the value of \\( y \\) in the given diagram, we need to understand the relationship between the angles and the circular arc.\n\n1. The diagram shows a circle with an arc that spans from \\( 90^\\circ \\) to \\( 360^\\circ \\).\n2. The angle \\( y^\\circ \\) is located at the center of the circle.\n3. The arc between the angles \\( 90^\\circ \\) and \\( 360^\\circ \\) is the entire circle, which is \\( 360^\\circ \\).\n\nSince the entire circle is \\( 360^\\circ \\), the angle \\( y^\\circ \\) must be the measure of the central angle that subtends the entire circle. This central angle is half of the total angle of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\( y^\\circ \\) is:\n\\[ y^\\circ = \\frac{360^\\circ}{2} = 180^\\circ \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( y \\) is \\( \\boxed{180} \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\( 180^\\circ \\). I hope it is correct."
