"To find the smallest possible product of one one-digit prime and two distinct two-digit primes, we need to identify the smallest one-digit prime number and the smallest two-digit prime numbers.\n\nThe smallest one-digit prime number is 2.\n\nThe smallest two-digit prime numbers are 11, 13, and 17.\n\nNow, we calculate the product of these numbers:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 11 \\times 13 \\times 17\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\( 2 \\times 11 \\):\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 11 = 22\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\( 22 \\times 13 \\):\n\n\\[\n22 \\times 13 = 286\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate \\( 286 \\times 17 \\):\n\n\\[\n286 \\times 17 = 4862\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible product of one one-digit prime and two distinct two-digit primes is \\( 4862.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is 4862. I hope it is correct."
