"To solve the equation \\(7 - 4x = 15\\), we first isolate the term involving \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7 - 4x = 15\n\\]\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n-4x = 15 - 7\n\\]\n\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n-4x = 8\n\\]\n\nNext, divide both sides by -4 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{8}{-4}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n\n\\[\nx = -2\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(x = -2\\), we substitute this value into the expression \\(8x + 2\\):\n\n\\[\n8x + 2 = 8(-2) + 2\n\\]\n\nCalculate the product:\n\n\\[\n8(-2) = -16\n\\]\n\nThen add 2:\n\n\\[\n-16 + 2 = -14\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(8x + 2\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-14}\n\\]"
